{"name":"Fancy Pants","hex":"#f3dae1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fancy pants","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person wearing fancy clothing; a member of a social elite.","A person very concerned with their appearance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy_pants"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fancy Pants (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fancy Pants is a 1950 American romantic comedy Western film directed by George Marshall and starring Bob Hope and Lucille Ball. It is a musical adaptation of Ruggles of Red Gap (1935)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Fancy_Pants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancy_Pants_(film)"},{"title":"Fancy Pants (video game series)","blocks":[{"text":"Fancy Pants is a series of free side-scrolling Flash games created by American developer Brad Borne. Four worlds have been released so far. World 1 was released on March 14, 2006 and World 2 was released on January 9, 2008. After the 2009 Comic-Con, Borne announced he would officially start working on World 3. It was released on April 5, 2012. A console version developed by Borne and Over the Top Games was released by EA 2D for PlayStation Network and Xbox Live Arcade on April 19 and April 20, 2011, respectively. An iOS version developed by Chillingo, Over the Top Games and Borne Games was released on Apple's App Store on March 4, 2012, with an Android version released on May 22, 2017. In 2017, Brad Borne made a fourth entry, Super Fancy Pants Adventure, which was later ported to Adobe Flash in 2020 as World 4."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fancy_Pants_(video_game_series)"},{"title":"Trousers","blocks":[{"text":"Trousers, slacks, or pants are an item of clothing worn from the waist to anywhere between the knees and the ankles, covering both legs separately .\nShorts are similar to trousers, but with legs that come down only as far as the knee, but may be considerably shorter depending on the style of the garment. To distinguish them from shorts, trousers may be called \"long trousers\" in certain contexts such as school uniform, where tailored shorts may be called \"short trousers\" in the UK."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Trousers-colourisolated.jpg/330px-Trousers-colourisolated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trousers"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Fancy_Pants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c7/Fancy_Pants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFancy_Pants.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cd/Newgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg/250px-Newgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cd/Newgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cd/Newgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg/250px-Newgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fancy Pants Man (left) fights against Newgrounds mascot Pico (middle) and Alien Hominid in Newgrounds Rumble.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANewgrounds_Rumble_Screenshot_Fancy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Trousers-colourisolated.jpg/500px-Trousers-colourisolated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Trousers-colouriso